  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 152 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nAbove normal temperatures are expected today through Thursday. \nRecord highs are possible Monday and Tuesday with upper 80s to low \n90s possible. A frontal system will slowly sink south into the area \nWednesday and will stall out across northern portions of the area \nbefore moving on as a cold front Thursday night. 20-30% shower and \nstorm chances infiltrate the northwest portions of the area Tuesday \nnight. Chances then increase throughout the day Wednesday from \nnorthwest to southeast to 60-80%, then dropping down to a near area \nwide 50-60% Wednesday evening and overnight. Chances then continue \non Thursday with a bit more of a gradient with 20-60% chances from \nsoutheast to northwest. Right now there are some early indications \nof the potential for severe weather along the frontal boundary and \nin the vicinity of the attendant sfc low, but uncertainty remains \nhigh at this point. Something to keep an eye on. Chances taper off \nby Friday morning. \n\nBehind the cold front are cooler temperatures for Friday through the \nweekend. Temperatures could be around 10 degrees below normal on \nSaturday, in the upper 50s to low 60s.",
